        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: garden city movement, urban planning, greenbelts\n- People: Sir Ebenezer Howard\n- Topics: self-contained communities, residences, industry, agriculture, publication\n\nFacts:\n- In 1898, Sir Ebenezer Howard initiated the garden city movement.\n- Sir Ebenezer Howard was born on 29 January 1850 and died on 1 May 1928.\n- Sir Ebenezer Howard was an English founder of the garden city movement.\n- The garden city movement is a method of urban planning.\n- The garden city movement proposes self-contained communities surrounded by greenbelts.\n- The garden city movement includes proportionate areas of residences, industry, and agriculture.\n- Sir Ebenezer Howard is known for a publication from 1898.",
